From 91b4d5fe3d81dba0d930f03b79fac3ae3ba09b3b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 22:34:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/20] Homes strips: one slow place no longer empties a page's
 strips; a slot that misses fills after load

Loris on the 13-town page (owner, 2026-11-08). Each place now answers on its own within the
page's 3-second budget. A slow search keeps going in the background (waitUntil), so its answer
is cached for the next reader, and the page fills the empty slot after load from
/homes/api/place (same search, bar and markup; no hearts; adds the listing notice if missing).

